# .goblin/loop/predicate — the loop's exit condition. Copy this file to that path and edit it.
#
# ONE command. Exits 0 == the loop is finished. Comments are allowed here; the command is the
# single non-blank, non-comment line (LP-01 checks exactly that).
#
# A duration is NOT a finish condition, and neither is a description of one.
# Run it once BEFORE iteration 1 and record the result in .goblin/loop/first-run as
# "exit=<n> ts=<ISO8601>": the run-once rule is how you know the command is runnable and
# currently red, which is what makes a later green mean anything.
# Then pin it: sha256sum .goblin/loop/predicate | cut -d' ' -f1 > .goblin/loop/predicate.sha256
# Never edit the predicate mid-loop — archive it under .goblin/loop/closed-<date>/ and open a
# new loop instead (LP-02).
#
# Replace the line below with the real condition. Example shape only:
node tools/check-cycles.mjs
